# SoC boot-args for the POCO F4 (munch, SM8250 "kona").
# Generated by devices/poco-f4/pull-soc.sh from the phone's /sys/firmware/fdt, with
# soc_aoss and soc_cmd_db added by hand (tools/soc-args.py misses them on kona — see below).
#
# Compared to redwood (SM7325 "yupik"), the addresses soc-args.py finds are IDENTICAL
# (same Qualcomm SoC block layout across these two families). The differences on munch are
# what the parser does NOT find:
#   - soc_aoss: munch's AOSS node is /soc/qcom,qmp-aop@c300000 (compatible qcom,sm8250-aoss-qmp,
#     not qcom,sm8350-aoss-qmp which soc-args.py looks for). Address 0xc300000 is the same as
#     redwood's; added by hand.
#   - soc_cmd_db: munch's reserved-memory node is "reserved-memory@80860000" (no "cmd_db" in
#     the name). Address 0x80860000 same as redwood's; added by hand.
#   - soc_mpss_mem: ABSENT on munch. The SM8250 split-modem architecture has no mpss/mss
#     reserved-memory node — the modem memory is managed differently (modem_pr/so/*.mbn,
#     not a monolithic modem.mdt loaded into a fixed region). hakios.mpss.c (written for
#     redwood's monolithic modem) will need rework for this. See devices/poco-f4/README.md.
soc_ipa_base=0x1e40000
soc_gsi_base=0x1e04000
soc_ipcc=0x408000
soc_aoss=0xc300000
soc_rsc=0x18220000
soc_apps_smmu=0x15000000
soc_cmd_db=0x80860000
soc_smem=0x80900000
soc_imem=0x14600000
